{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1043 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "93e55063951e8ba11589a205045f353cdd3a397a7579752b1cb491f5648d3e74" :edb/db-before-t 1042 :edb/db-after-t 1043 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534355 50 #inst "2026-10-06T16:43:24.952Z" 13194139534355 true] [17592186100868 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283962 13194139534355 true] [17592186100868 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283969 13194139534355 true] [17592186100876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283955 13194139534355 true] [17592186100876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283972 13194139534355 true] [17592186101071 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534355 false] [17592186101071 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534355 true] [17592186101071 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y=-2{e}^{-2x}$\n- $y=-2{e}^{x}$\n- $y=2{e}^{-x}+1$" 13194139534355 true] [17592186101071 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} =-2y$.\n\nWhich of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n1. $y =-2e^{-2x}$\n2. $y =-2e^{x}$\n3. $y = 2e^{-x} + 1$" 13194139534355 false] [17592186101071 1145 "Check the derivative against $-2y$ for each candidate.\n\n- I: $y=-2e^{-2x}$ gives $y'=4e^{-2x}=-2y$, so it is a solution.\n- II: $y=-2e^x$ gives $y'=-2e^x$, whereas $-2y=4e^x$, so it fails.\n- III: $y=2e^{-x}+1$ gives $y'=-2e^{-x}$, whereas $-2y=-4e^{-x}-2$, so it fails.\n\nSelect **I only**." 13194139534355 false] [17592186101071 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=-2{e}^{-2x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{-2x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ 4{e}^{-2x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(-2{e}^{-2x}) \\\\ 4{e}^{-2x} & =4{e}^{-2x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-2{e}^{-2x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-2{e}^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ -2{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(-2{e}^{x}) \\\\ -2{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}4{e}^{x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 6{e}^{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=-2{e}^{x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2{e}^{-x}+1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ -2{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(2{e}^{-x}+1) \\\\ -2{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-4{e}^{-x}-2 \\\\ 2{e}^{-x} & \\ne -2.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2{e}^{-x}+1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283955 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283956 13194139534355 true] [17592186283955 1089 "q-141091" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283955 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534355 true] [17592186283955 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$\n- $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1$\n- $y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283955 1113 #uuid "a471fc2f-d62d-516e-bc45-9db90390f695" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283955 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1)\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 0 & =2\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283957 13194139534355 true] [17592186283956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283958 13194139534355 true] [17592186283956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283959 13194139534355 true] [17592186283956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283960 13194139534355 true] [17592186283956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283961 13194139534355 true] [17592186283956 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534355 true] [17592186283956 1041 "selection" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283956 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283957 13194139534355 true] [17592186283956 1110 #uuid "8d9dfc3b-5a30-52b4-9822-c3c4b31eb052" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283957 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283957 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534355 true] [17592186283957 1111 #uuid "2e143d2f-ee04-5895-b088-8261f80d40f6" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283958 1034 "I only" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283958 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534355 true] [17592186283958 1111 #uuid "19de3e4b-1afd-5bdb-9c4d-2e62671615a4" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283959 1034 "III only" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283959 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534355 true] [17592186283959 1111 #uuid "fc6b3f5c-d6da-5869-963a-d587df226830" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283960 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283960 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534355 true] [17592186283960 1111 #uuid "2e86f126-5240-5cb2-b281-3d3521c0921f" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283961 1034 "II only" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283961 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534355 true] [17592186283961 1111 #uuid "d36bb8a4-5040-5b18-9dd1-e0abab000047" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283962 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283963 13194139534355 true] [17592186283962 1089 "q-141112" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283962 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534355 true] [17592186283962 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{y}{x},\\,y(-2)=-1.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=\\frac{A}{x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283962 1113 #uuid "8abc10be-3eb5-5e2c-9a94-244a431b287a" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283962 1145 "We're given that $y=\\frac{A}{x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(-2)=-1.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(-2)=-1$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{A}{x} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{A}{(-2)} \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{x}.\n$$" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283963 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283964 13194139534355 true] [17592186283963 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283965 13194139534355 true] [17592186283963 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283966 13194139534355 true] [17592186283963 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283967 13194139534355 true] [17592186283963 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283968 13194139534355 true] [17592186283963 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534355 true] [17592186283963 1041 "selection" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283963 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283965 13194139534355 true] [17592186283963 1110 #uuid "b4c02ff0-537c-5ba7-ae43-ff24f564feb7" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283964 1034 "-\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283964 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534355 true] [17592186283964 1111 #uuid "01b61262-b1e1-5209-b2da-3fc98cfc53df" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283965 1034 "2" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283965 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534355 true] [17592186283965 1111 #uuid "dfb65e36-c318-5026-b6b2-c21070996b82" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283966 1034 "1" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283966 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534355 true] [17592186283966 1111 #uuid "9b0dc2d5-2892-5706-96b9-cbb4a702ce44" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283967 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283967 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534355 true] [17592186283967 1111 #uuid "a34cfbee-5c94-5162-9256-80942a66612e" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283968 1034 "-1" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283968 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534355 true] [17592186283968 1111 #uuid "5a9dd988-3928-5bba-9fa6-088dfac520fe" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283969 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283970 13194139534355 true] [17592186283969 1089 "q-352663" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283969 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534355 true] [17592186283969 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3y}{x},\\,y(2)=4.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=A{x}^{3}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283969 1113 #uuid "d60af566-8837-57e8-b627-8477d386c176" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283969 1145 "We're given that $y=A{x}^{3}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(2)=4.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(2)=4$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{x}^{3} \\\\ 4 & =A(2)^{3} \\\\ 4 & =A(8) \\\\ A & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283970 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283971 13194139534355 true] [17592186283970 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534355 true] [17592186283970 1041 "field-1" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283970 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283971 13194139534355 true] [17592186283970 1110 #uuid "2d8a6415-b53e-54f5-8a38-a2cb50262b52" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283971 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283971 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534355 true] [17592186283971 1111 #uuid "0c4c2eb4-efdf-5a11-ae1d-d488e5cfce93" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283972 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283973 13194139534355 true] [17592186283972 1089 "q-79333" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283972 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534355 true] [17592186283972 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y=\\frac{7}{x}$\n- $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$\n- $y=\\frac{2}{x}$" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283972 1113 #uuid "026a0cae-bdc3-5eb5-888c-83ba0c1115ea" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283972 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\frac{7}{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{(\\frac{7}{x})}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}} & =-\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=\\frac{7}{x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-\\frac{1}{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{x})}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=\\frac{2}{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{(\\frac{2}{x})}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=\\frac{2}{x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283974 13194139534355 true] [17592186283973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283975 13194139534355 true] [17592186283973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283976 13194139534355 true] [17592186283973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283977 13194139534355 true] [17592186283973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283978 13194139534355 true] [17592186283973 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534355 true] [17592186283973 1041 "selection" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283973 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283974 13194139534355 true] [17592186283973 1110 #uuid "3db0b1ef-c8dc-580f-8d9d-3d36b51250fe" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283974 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283974 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534355 true] [17592186283974 1111 #uuid "e2982eb2-2159-59db-9ba1-3b0538fe51a6" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283975 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283975 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534355 true] [17592186283975 1111 #uuid "34c1ba00-0e56-5150-9cab-44a2b3259f6d" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283976 1034 "III only" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283976 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534355 true] [17592186283976 1111 #uuid "84d06fc0-4ed4-560c-8333-af3559a8f046" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283977 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283977 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534355 true] [17592186283977 1111 #uuid "1ceb600f-0104-52b3-ab17-027a337a6cd0" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283978 1034 "II only" 13194139534355 true] [17592186283978 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534355 true] [17592186283978 1111 #uuid "8969a8b6-7e3b-5c4d-b05f-c8c253f7596e" 13194139534355 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-141091" 17592186283955 "q-141091/selection" 17592186283956 "q-141091/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" 17592186283957 "q-141091/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" 17592186283958 "q-141091/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51